00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:21,000
Partner up!

2
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Pokémon Detective Pikachu is a action, adventure,
fantasy film directed by Rob Letterman.

3
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:51,000
In a world where people collect pocket-size monsters (Pokémon) to do battle, a boy
comes across an intelligent monster who seeks to be a detective.

4
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Detective Pikachu (voice), played by Ryan Reynolds.

5
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Tim Goodman, played by Justice Smith.

6
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Lucy Stevens, played by Kathryn Newton.

7
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:51,000
Ms. Norman, played by Suki Waterhouse.

8
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Sebastian, played by Omar Chaparro.

9
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:21,000
Roger Clifford, played by Chris Geere.

10
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
Pokémon Detective Pikachu is a 2019 fantasy comedy film and the
first live-action film based on the Pokémon franchise.

11
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:51,000
It is a loose adaptation of the 2016 video game Detective Pikachu.

12
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Directed by Rob Letterman, who co-wrote it with Dan Hernandez, Benji Samit, and Derek Connolly, the film stars Ryan Reynolds as the voice and motion capture
of Pikachu, with Justice Smith, Kathryn Newton, Suki Waterhouse, Omar Chaparro, Chris Geere, Ken Watanabe and Bill Nighy in live-action roles.

13
01:08:15,000 --> 01:08:21,000
The plot follows Detective Pikachu and his partner Tim Goodman as they attempt
to solve the mysterious disappearance of Tim's father, Harry.

14
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
Filming took place from January to May 2018 in Colorado, England, and Scotland.

15
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:51,000
Detective Pikachu was released in Japan on May 3, 2019, and in
the United States on May 10, by Warner Bros.

16
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and grossed $433 million against a $150
million budget, becoming the second-highest grossing video game film adaptation at the time.

17
01:29:15,000 --> 01:29:21,000
A sequel is in development.

18
01:34:30,000 --> 01:34:36,000
The film explores themes of amnesia, detective, car
crash, whodunit, based on video game.

19
01:39:45,000 --> 01:39:51,000
The tone is dark.
